    {
      "heading": "About the pronunciations",
      "text": [
        "Pronunciations follow standard Budapest Hungarian, written as exact (bracketed) IPA. Spelling is almost perfectly phonetic, and the stress always falls on the first syllable (ˈ). An accent mark on a vowel makes it long, and a doubled consonant is held longer (kettő [ˈkɛtːøː]). Endings follow vowel harmony: back-vowel words take back-vowel endings (házak), front-vowel words front ones (kertek)."
      ]
    },
